# Production build for https://ddinovstravel.uz
#
# Both values are deliberately EMPTY, which makes the client fall back to the relative
# paths /api and /api/media/upload (see src/services/api.js). Calling its own origin means
# the site works on ddinovstravel.uz and www.ddinovstravel.uz alike, over either scheme,
# and never trips CORS — the browser sees no cross-origin request at all.
#
# This assumes the web server in front of the site proxies /api to the Spring Boot app,
# e.g. in nginx:
#
#   location /api/ { proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/; }
#
# If the API instead lives on its own host, put the absolute base here and make sure the
# site's origin is listed in the backend's CORS_ORIGINS:
#
#   VITE_API_URL=https://api.ddinovstravel.uz/api
#   VITE_UPLOAD_URL=https://api.ddinovstravel.uz/api/media/upload
VITE_API_URL=
VITE_UPLOAD_URL=
